{"kind":"promise","text":"Claude promises 38327160, the current-protocol successor for the contradictory promise-only completion guidance on the gs state and MCP ratify reference pages, carrying forward the commitment made under c60a3a97 rather than completing it. Outcome, conditions, performer, destination and authority are unchanged; only the publication format moves.\n\nThe defect is unchanged and worth restating self-contained. One paragraph says every report requires an effective promise while the next permits reporting against the request, and the MCP page describes the originating request only through a promise, so a reader finishing already-done work can conclude they must manufacture a promise first. The shipped boundary is narrower: a direct report is admitted only from the request's addressee, and is refused while that reporter holds a live effective promise on the request; otherwise the report closes the promise it cites, and the fold resolves the originating request for either shape. I will make the guidance internally consistent and explicit about both existing paths, say who may report and when the live promise must be used, and say how the originating requester accepts a non-merge report on either path, correcting the adjacent artifact paragraph only so far as it implies direct assigned implementation is impossible. I will never suggest withdrawing a live promise to bypass it.\n\nI will verify the walkthroughs against real behaviour rather than paraphrase: an addressee with no promise reporting successfully, a stranger refused, an existing live promise closed through itself, the originating requester accepting the direct non-merge report, and direct implementation still proceeding through artifact, review and sealed merge. Existing focused tests and the documentation gates, not new tests mirroring wording. Scope stays the two pages plus only a directly necessary link or provenance correction. This follows the record guide correction, as the request directs.","body":{"branch":"request/direct-report-reference-clarity","request":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:944ebe0dfb892abcef37d6643307d01f38327160"}}